 Today's newsletter is 777 words, a 3-minute read. 

 📉 The dashboard: The S&amp;P 500 closed down 0.4%.

 The index gained 0.1% for the week and is up 12.8% for the year. 🥶 Today's stock spotlight: Fair Isaac Corp. (-16.7%), the company behind the FICO score, tumbled after Federal Housing Finance Agency director Bill Pulte directed Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac to start accepting a rival credit score, escalating his monthslong criticism of the company's pricing.

 
 
